    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA Stokes Quirke are delighted to bring to the market this well-presented three bedroom semi detached residence, conveniently located in Ivowen in the popular village of Kilsheelan. The property is presented in good condition throughout and offers bright, comfortable accommodation comprising an entrance hall, living room, kitchen/dining area, three bedrooms and three bathrooms. Externally, the property benefits from off-street parking together with garden space. Kilsheelan is a highly sought-after village situated between Clonmel and Carrick-on-Suir, with a range of local amenities including a shop, school, pub and sporting facilities, while Clonmel is within easy commuting distance. This property would make an ideal family home or investment opportunity. Early viewing is recommended. \n\nAccommodation\n\nEntrance Hall\n1.75m x 5.60m Tiled flooring with a feature carpet staircase and a W.C under the stairs.\n\nWC\n1.37m x 1.50m Tiled flooring, W.C, W.H.B\n\nSitting Room\n2.75m x 4.85m Timber flooring, open fireplace and a window overlooking the front garden\n\nKitchen/Dining Room\n3.50m x 5.30m Tiled flooring and backsplash with units at eye and floor level. It benefits from a rear sliding door to the enclosed garden.\n\nFirst Floor\n\n\nLanding\n2.90m x 2.37m Carpet flooring with the Hotpress thereof.\n\nBathroom\n1.25m x 2.10m Tiled floor to ceiling with a W.C, W.H.B, bath and shower\n\nBedroom 1\n3.95m x 2.95m Carpet flooring, built in wardrobes and a window overlooking the rear garden. Benefiting from an En-Suite\n\nEn-suite\n2.35m x 1.20m Tiled flooring, W.C, W.H.B and shower\n\nBedroom 2\n2.90m x 3.50m Carpet flooring, built in wardrobes and a window overlooking the front garden\n\nBedroom 3\n3.60m x 2.23m Carpet flooring, built in wardrobes and a window overlooking the front garden\n\n\nOutside\nExternally, the property benefits from off-street parking together with a private garden, offering a pleasant and practical outdoor space."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Presented in good condition throughout\nC BER rating\nOff-street parking\nConvenient village location\nWithin easy commuting distance of Clonmel and Carrick-on-Suir\n \n Oil-fired central heating with mains water and sewage \n Kilsheelan offers a range of local amenities including a primary school, shop, pubs, church and sporting facilities, with a wider selection of shops, schools and services available in nearby Clonmel."
      },
